Subject: [adegenet-forum] bug in version 1.2-0
Message-ID: <1216229498.487e307a568b0@webmail.univ-lyon1.fr>

Dear list,

Denis Laloe pointed out a nasty bug in version 1.2-0: when importing data, NAs
are not taken into account when coded as series of zeros ("000000"), which is
the case in the genetix format for instance. Instead, "000000" was interpreted
as an homozygote for allele "000". This is fixed in the devel version (likely
available from R-Forge tomorrow). There is also a patch against import.R
available from the website (section 'Download').

Sorry for this inconvenience.

Best,

Thibaut.

